# Typography System — Virelle

Applies with `design/design-system.mdc`. Typography creates hierarchy and brand voice — not decoration.

Source of truth: Google Fonts link in HTML + usage in SCSS blocks (`Cormorant Garamond`, `Montserrat`). Prefer introducing `--font-display` / `--font-body` tokens in `_variables.scss` when touching type systematically.

## Product context

| Cue | Direction |
|-----|-----------|
| Audience | Shoppers scanning beauty + comfort |
| Language | Russian — fonts must cover Cyrillic well |
| Voice | Elegant display personality in headings; clean UI in body |

## Font families (fixed)

| Role | Family |
|------|--------|
| Display / brand / headings | **Cormorant Garamond** |
| Body / UI / controls | **Montserrat** |

```css
font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; /* headings, logo, hero */
font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif;    /* body, buttons, meta */
```

**Rule:** Cormorant for brand, hero title, section titles, product names where already used; Montserrat for body, nav actions, buttons, filters. Do not add a third family without an explicit request. Keep `display=swap` on font loads.

## Scale & roles

Prefer consistent sizes via tokens/utilities over one-off `px` when extending the system.

| Role | Typical use |
|------|-------------|
| Hero / brand H1 | `Virelle` — strongest display |
| Hero subtitle | Short category line (пижамы и бельё) |
| Section H2 | `.section-title` |
| Section support | `.section-subtitle` |
| Product name | `.product-name` |
| Body | Descriptions, about, testimonials |
| Price / meta | `.product-price`, badges, helper text |

## Hierarchy

On every section the user must instantly see: topic (H2), product/proof, optional CTA. Do not make every line visually equal.

Build hierarchy from **size + weight + spacing + color** — not color alone. Text colors from `--color-text-*` / gold utility (`.text-gold`).

## Heading structure (a11y)

- One **H1** on the page (hero brand)
- Sections: **H2** (`.section-title`)
- Cards / items: **H3/H4** as already patterned — don’t skip levels for styling

## Weight, line height, tracking

- Cormorant: lighter elegant weights for large display; avoid heavy bold everywhere
- Montserrat: 300–500 for UI; reserve 600 for emphasis
- Headings: tighter line-height; body: comfortable reading
- Hero title: balanced wrap; don’t let brand wrap awkwardly on mobile

## Density & responsive

Mobile-first: readable base, no overflow, clear hierarchy. Check catalog filters and product grids at narrow widths.

## Accessibility

Support zoom and contrast. Avoid tiny muted-on-muted prices/labels and image-only critical copy.

## Output Format (new system / audit)

1. **Font strategy** — families, Cyrillic, performance
2. **Scale** — size / weight / line-height per role
3. **Tokens** — preferred `--font-*` / size variables if introducing them

## Implementation Order

1. Tokens (if any) → 2. Global/base → 3. Section & product type → 4. Responsive → 5. a11y

For audits, follow `design/ui-review.mdc`.
